For instance:

You have a table tDialog, fields  inFunctionFrom, inFunctionTo and 
inDialogNum (all INTEGER). inFunctionFrom and  inFunctionTo are FK fields.
  In table tFunction you can find the titles of the functions, the titles 
related to inFunctionFrom and  inFunctionTo you want to see in your 
dynbrowser instance. So you create two calc-fields in the SDO and write 
functions to get these titles. In 9.1A you need to rewrite the generated 
data.calculate so that every assign is separated, to eliminate compile-error
196 with the generated data.calculate procedure caused by the preprocessor 
(needed for an index-supported search) you define in the definitionssection
of your SDO:

&SCOPED-DEFINE rowobjindex INDEX TitleFrom calc INDEX TitleTo calc-2

PROCEDURE DATA.CALCULATE :
/*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Purpose:     Calculate all the Calculated Expressions found in the
               SmartDataObject.
  Parameters:  <none>
------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
 rowObject.CALC = TitleFrom().
 rowObject.CALC-2 = TitleTo().
END PROCEDURE.

If you want to sort on CALC fields, you need to provide a
rowidWhereoverride of rowidWhere in the SDO, in this example:

FUNCTION rowidWhere RETURNS CHARACTER
  ( INPUT pcWhere AS CHARACTER) :
/*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Purpose:     Super Override
  Notes:       
------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

  /* Code placed here will execute PRIOR to standard behavior. */

  DEFINE VARIABLE rCustomRowid        AS ROWID   NO-UNDO.
  DEFINE VARIABLE cRowids             AS CHAR    NO-UNDO.
  DEFINE VARIABLE cSearchFld          AS CHAR    NO-UNDO.
  DEFINE VARIABLE cDataQuerySort      AS CHAR    NO-UNDO.
  DEFINE VARIABLE iRecord             AS INT     NO-UNDO.
  DEFINE VARIABLE iTarget             AS INT     NO-UNDO.
  DEFINE VARIABLE hTarget             AS HANDLE  NO-UNDO.  
  DEFINE VARIABLE hBrowse             AS HANDLE  NO-UNDO.   
 
  {get DataQuerySort cDataQuerySort}.
  ASSIGN cSearchFld = REPLACE(cDataQuerySort,'BY':U,'':U). 
         cSearchFld = TRIM(cSearchFld).
  
  FOR EACH tFunction NO-LOCK WHERE 
     tFunction.chtitle >= TRIM(ENTRY(2,REPLACE(pcWhere,'~'':U,'':U),'=':U)),
    EACH tDialog NO-LOCK WHERE 
      IF cSearchFld = 'CALC':u THEN tDialog.inFunctionFrom = tFunction.inFunction
      ELSE /* CALC-2 */ tDialog.inFunctionTo = tFunction.inFunction:
      ASSIGN rCustomRowid = ROWID(tDialog)
             cRowids      = IF cRowids NE '' THEN cRowids + ',' + STRING(rCustomRowid)
                            ELSE STRING(rCustomRowid)
             iRecord      = iRecord + 1.
    IF iRecord = 200 THEN LEAVE. /* Make sure cRowids is not blown up */
  END.
  IF cRowids NE '' THEN {set CustomRowidString cRowids}.

 RETURN SUPER( INPUT pcWhere ).

END FUNCTION.

override of initializeObject:

PROCEDURE initializeObject:
  DEFINE VARIABLE cDataQuerySort   AS CHARACTER NO-UNDO.
  DEFINE VARIABLE cDataQueryString AS CHARACTER NO-UNDO.
  /* Code placed here will execute PRIOR to standard behavior. */

  cDataQuerySort = ' BY CALC':U.
  {set DataQuerySort cDataQuerySort}. 

  {get DataQueryString cDataQueryString}. 
  ASSIGN cDataQueryString = IF INDEX(cDataQueryString,"INDEXED-REPOSITION":U) NE 0 THEN
                              REPLACE(cDataQueryString,"INDEXED-REPOSITION":U,'':U)
                            ELSE cDataQueryString.
  {set DataQueryString cDataQueryString}.  


  /* Code placed here will execute PRIOR to standard behavior. */

  RUN SUPER.

  /* Code placed here will execute AFTER standard behavior.    */

END PROCEDURE.

The where clause you are generating in rowidWhere with the rowids is 
expensive. If you know a better solution or have other remarks, please 
send it to me and I'll upgrade the zipfile.
Don't forget to place all adm2-customcode in customdirectories.

